                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Classic Bitmap Brother's retro-gaming steampunk co-op goodness, but a mixed re-release.\n\nThings to be aware of:\n- Other than a bloom effect on select sprites (shots, explosions, etc) this pretty much identical to an emulator experience. This release isn't bringing anything new to the table.\n- Colour differences between the original Amiga (more muted) and the PC versions can be divisive. So if you grew up on the Amiga version that could be an obstacle.\n- It's a hard game and there's no difficulty selection on the PC version (this was only a feature in the SNES version I believe).\n- The Mac binary is 32bit only so won't run on any current version of macOS and the Windows version won't run through Crossover. Ironically meaning it's easier to run the original than this updated version.\n\nAnyway, hopefully some of that was useful.",
